<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    angr short-circuit condition folding across a COMPLEX sibling, the GUARD
    CASCADE shape: `option condfold off|on|wide` (default-OFF; ELEM 4113), S8
    goto-quality sub-stage.  Closes proposal #56 (lighttpd server.c::main in the
    angr corpus binary `newbury` @0x40f696, which reaches 0 gotos / 0 labels
    with this option on, down from 1 / 1).

    This witness folds through RULE A; the Rule-B isolation lives in
    tests/stages/ghangr-condfold-ruleb.xml.  See WHICH RULE FIRES below.

    THE SHAPE.  A short-circuit permission guard whose arms reconverge on one
    shared body:

      B0: if (uid() == 0)          -> BODY  else B1
      B1: if (euid() != want_uid)  -> BAD   else B2
      B2: if (egid() != want_gid)  -> BAD   else BODY
      BAD:  r = -1; warn();  -> RET   (in-degree 2: B1, B2)
      BODY: setup(); run() x13; r = 0;  -> RET   (in-degree 2: B0, B2)

    Every gate of CollapseStructure::ruleBlockOr holds for (B1,B2) and then for
    (B0, B1||B2) EXCEPT one: BlockBasic::isComplex.  That predicate calls a
    block complex once its statement count exceeds 2, and a clause block holding
    a call plus its branch plus one more statement is already at 3.  So the fold
    is declined, the cascade is left to the if/sequence schemas, and one of the
    two edges into BODY must be virtualized: kuna emits a forward "goto label_X"
    out of one arm plus a "label_X:" inside the sibling arm.  angr emits
    neither, because when its _match_acyclic_short_circuit_conditions hits a
    non-single-statement operand it wraps the operand in a
    MultiStatementExpression instead of declining.

    THE FIX.  option condfold relaxes that one gate.  kuna's printer already
    renders a folded BlockCondition's second operand under
    modifiers::COMMA_SEPARATE (emit_basic_block_ops walks EVERY op in the block
    and emits them comma-separated with the semicolon suppressed), so nothing is
    dropped - isComplex is a readability budget, not a correctness gate.  With
    the option on the cascade folds into one compound condition and BODY becomes
    the fall-through join.

    NO REORDERING IS POSSIBLE.  new_block_condition only relabels two blocks
    that are ALREADY sequenced in the CFG as the left and right operands of a
    "&amp;&amp;" / "||".  C short-circuits left to right and the comma operator
    sequences left to right, so the emitted expression evaluates B1's statements
    and condition and then - only if the short circuit does not cut - B2's.
    That is the CFG's own order and conditionality, which is why predicates that
    call functions need no purity analysis.  See p8_structure/kuna_condfold.rs.

    WHICH LEVEL, AND WHY `wide`.  Both admission rules sit on top of ONE shared
    printed-width budget: the folded operand may render at most 5 comma elements
    at `on` and 9 at `wide`, measured by kuna_condfold.rs (printed_shape) with
    the printer's own skip rules.  On THIS vehicle the stub callees have no
    prototype and no frame recovery, so each guard block still carries the
    call's stack-effect ops (INT_ADD / STORE / LOAD around the CALL) when
    structuring runs, and printed_shape measures 6 for a block whose operand
    finally emits none.  The measure over-counts, which only ever declines a
    fold - so this witness needs `wide`, while the REAL newbury::main (whose
    libc calls are prototyped) measures 3 per guard block and closes at `on`.
    That is deliberate and is itself the two-pass proof of the shared budget:
    under the pre-review code, where Rule B had no width cap at all, this shape
    folded at `on`.

    WHICH RULE FIRES.  Rule A, both times.  `condfold`'s admission predicate is
    the UNION of two rules and condfold_ok consults Rule A first; at `wide` Rule
    A's budget also admits these guard blocks (measured with
    KUNA_CONDFOLD_DEBUG=1: 2 `prefix` folds per engine, 0 `shape`), so this
    witness proves the guard-cascade SHAPE folds end to end but does NOT isolate
    Rule B.  Deleting Rule B would leave it green.  Rule B is isolated by the
    third condfold witness, tests/stages/ghangr-condfold-ruleb.xml, whose middle
    guard holds two statement-root calls and is therefore outside Rule A's
    MAX_PREFIX_ROOT_CALLS = 1 at every level; the companion witness
    tests/stages/ghangr-condfold.xml exercises Rule A on its own.

    WITNESS.  Self-contained, no relocations: gcc -O2 output for

      int f(int argc, int uid, int gid) {
        int r;
        if (su_uid() == 0 || (su_euid() == uid &amp;&amp; su_egid() == gid)) {
          su_setup(); su_run(argc+0) ... su_run(argc+11); r = 0;
        } else { r = -1; su_warn(); }
        return r;
      }

    with every callee a local stub in the same chunk (no PLT, no data
    references).  The body is 13 calls wide so the default-on taildup does not
    duplicate it away - taildup only removes this goto for a tiny tail.

    Pass 1 (option condfold off): the fold is declined and one edge into the
    shared body is virtualized - "goto" appears exactly once, and so does the
    "label_" prefix of its target line.
    Pass 2 (option condfold wide): the cascade folds, so neither token appears
    in the second pass, and the de Morgan orientation ruleBlockOr applies turns
    the two equality guards into the inverted disjunction "su_euid() != " that
    guards the terminating arm.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000">

</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="su_uid"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100010" name="su_euid"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100020" name="su_egid"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100030" name="su_warn"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100040" name="su_setup"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100050" name="su_run"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100060" name="f"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option condfold off</com>
  <com>lo fu f</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option condfold wide</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="condfold-newbury #1: OFF virtualizes one of the two edges into the shared body to a goto; WIDE folds the cascade so no goto is emitted" min="1" max="1">goto</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="condfold-newbury #2: OFF must also emit the goto's target label inside the sibling arm; WIDE emits no label" min="1" max="1">label_[0-9a-f]+:</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="condfold-newbury #3: WIDE folds the two equality guards into one inverted short-circuit condition guarding the terminating arm" min="1" max="1">su_euid\(\) != </stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="condfold-newbury #4: OFF keeps the guards positive and nested (the un-inverted form appears only in the OFF pass, the WIDE pass has none)" min="1" max="1">su_euid\(\) == </stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
